# The refutations of the binary naturals' candidacy, as prolog_backend_shapes
# writes the unary naturals', the booleans' and the lists': a candidate class
# for `binary_set true` is refuted when one layer of its own structure differs
# from the binary naturals' shape (three alternatives, the first with no
# field, the other two with one field each; binary_wren_shapes), or when the
# shape's second or third field is refuted for them in turn. Refutation is a
# least fixed point read bottom up, so a candidate that no layer
# contradicts, a cycle through the shape included, is never refuted. A
# mismatch is written for a candidate only, as the unify node of the
# candidacy and the refutation beside the candidacy; the field refutations,
# as shapes_natural_field_refuted, need no candidacy on their left side.
# Every lemma here only adds, and none reads a function type: a binary
# natural is a Scott value, whose type may also hold one
# (https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/2188).
#
# A separate module, so that binary_wren_shapes, which other presets select,
# keeps its readings; wren_elimination_preset's type check selects it.
#
# Every lemma is sound by the section zero_universe: both sides are
# candidate, refuted and unify applied to all their arguments, each 0 by
# Lemma Z of that proof, and their choices 0 by the unit law, whatever the
# arguments.
